  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith (Site Location Plan, 101.01, 101.02, 101.03 and 101.04; received 19 November 2012; received 19 November 2012) and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - Unless within 3 months of the date of this decision a scheme for the provision of a minimum of 18 cycle parking spaces , unless a lower number is otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority, and a Travel Plan Statement that aims to promote sustainable travel to staff and students and improve access for pedestrians and cyclists, is submitted in writing to the Local Planning Authority for approval, and unless the approved scheme is implemented within 3 months of the Local Planning Authority's approval, the use of the site for non-residential education and training purposes shall cease until such time as a scheme is approved and implemented.",
    "Condition : 4 - The use hereby permitted for business (B1) purposes and non-residential education and training (D1) purposes shall not be carried on outside the following times:\r\n\r\n8:00am-8:00pm Monday to Saturday.\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987, as amended, or in any provision equivalent to that Class in any statutory instrument revoking and re-enacting that Order with or without modification; the premises shall only be used for business purposes (B1) and non-residential education and training purposes, excluding infant primary or secondary schools, and shall not be used for any other purpose within Use Class D1 without further approval in writing from the Local Planning Authority."
